00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:00:04,676 --> 00:00:06,111
If you want to get her to study,

2
00:00:06,177 --> 00:00:08,279
you'll be better off throwing away
the textbooks altogether.

3
00:00:08,346 --> 00:00:09,280
Excuse me?

4
00:00:09,347 --> 00:00:11,950
While you're here,
only do things that you think are fun.

5
00:00:12,016 --> 00:00:12,951
What's with that guy?

6
00:00:13,017 --> 00:00:16,121
<i>He's got a super naive mindset,</i>
<i>but is he all right?</i>

7
00:00:16,187 --> 00:00:17,122
Tatsuki.

8
00:00:17,188 --> 00:00:18,590
‎PREVIOUSLY ON <i>‎TATSUKI: TOO KIND FOR SCHOOL</i>

9
00:00:18,656 --> 00:00:19,757
I don't

10
00:00:20,925 --> 00:00:22,060
want to go to school.

11
00:00:22,127 --> 00:00:23,495
I think Ayaka couldn't

12
00:00:24,062 --> 00:00:25,797
bring herself to express her true feelings

13
00:00:25,864 --> 00:00:28,099
because her mother is so important to her.

14
00:00:28,166 --> 00:00:29,767
I was always

15
00:00:31,035 --> 00:00:33,438
a little too relieved whenever…

16
00:00:34,572 --> 00:00:35,874
you went to school, huh?

17
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,242
I'm sorry.

18
00:00:38,843 --> 00:00:40,178
-Hello?
<i>-Tatsuki.</i>

19
00:00:40,245 --> 00:00:41,813
Sora jumped.

20
00:00:43,148 --> 00:00:44,048
What?

21
00:00:48,353 --> 00:00:49,354
How's Sora?

22
00:00:53,825 --> 00:00:54,792
Is he in there?

23
00:00:55,593 --> 00:00:56,628
Wait.

24
00:00:57,595 --> 00:00:58,696
It's all right.

25
00:00:59,898 --> 00:01:02,700
-But he jumped--
-He's not in a critical condition.

26
00:01:04,302 --> 00:01:05,170
So just leave.

27
00:01:07,105 --> 00:01:08,439
Now.

28
00:01:32,564 --> 00:01:34,365
Tatsuki.

29
00:01:39,637 --> 00:01:40,705
He's sleeping.

30
00:01:45,076 --> 00:01:46,744
What? What is it?

31
00:01:46,811 --> 00:01:47,979
It's time for the meeting.

32
00:01:48,046 --> 00:01:49,814
-Meeting?
-Yeah.

33
00:01:49,881 --> 00:01:50,715
Okay.

34
00:01:51,382 --> 00:01:54,252
All right,
let's begin this week's meeting.

35
00:01:54,319 --> 00:01:56,087
-Okay.
-Okay.

36
00:01:56,154 --> 00:01:57,589
First up, Tuesday.

37
00:01:57,655 --> 00:02:00,291
There's a plan to go see the movie <i>Mario,</i>

38
00:02:00,358 --> 00:02:01,559
but is everyone done signing up?

39
00:02:01,626 --> 00:02:03,194
-I'll go too.
-Okay.

40
00:02:03,261 --> 00:02:06,030
-I'll sign up too.
-Let's watch a romantic comedy.

41
00:02:06,097 --> 00:02:08,132
-Romantic comedy?
-I have an idea for the next

42
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:09,334
-training camp.
-Training camp?

43
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,769
I want to eat paella this week.

44
00:02:11,836 --> 00:02:13,905
-Paella?
-Yes, paella.

45
00:02:13,972 --> 00:02:15,773
Paella!

46
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:19,444
Hold on, we're still discussing the movie.
We'll talk about the paella later.

47
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:21,512
We hold a meeting like this every week

48
00:02:21,579 --> 00:02:23,014
to decide on various plans.

49
00:02:23,615 --> 00:02:25,350
Do I need to take charge or anything?

50
00:02:25,416 --> 00:02:26,451
No need.

51
00:02:26,517 --> 00:02:28,486
We just need to watch over them.

52
00:02:29,053 --> 00:02:30,521
Everything works out all right?

53
00:02:31,089 --> 00:02:33,091
They won't follow plans made by adults,

54
00:02:33,157 --> 00:02:36,194
but they'll stick to the ones
they decided on themselves.

55
00:02:36,261 --> 00:02:37,495
-I see.
-Next.

56
00:02:37,562 --> 00:02:41,032
What's the plan for Thursday's
Activity Day at the community center?

57
00:02:41,099 --> 00:02:42,467
-Tag.
-Dodgeball.

58
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:43,701
-Tag?
-Basketball!

59
00:02:43,768 --> 00:02:45,603
-Yeah, basketball.
-Paella.

60
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:47,372
-Dodgeball?
-Enough with the paella.

61
00:02:47,438 --> 00:02:49,974
-Yeah, I want to do that too.
-Okay, let's vote.

62
00:02:50,041 --> 00:02:51,476
Who wants to play tag?

63
00:02:51,542 --> 00:02:54,178
-Me.
-Who wants to play basketball?

64
00:02:54,245 --> 00:02:56,347
-Me.
-What?

65
00:02:56,414 --> 00:02:57,749
Hold on, guys.

66
00:02:57,815 --> 00:02:59,083
You can only vote once.

67
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:00,518
We're not doing that.

68
00:03:00,585 --> 00:03:03,588
-I vote for dodgeball.
-I want to eat paella.

69
00:03:03,655 --> 00:03:06,524
-Who wants to do trampoline?
-I think it's a new applicant.

70
00:03:07,558 --> 00:03:08,760
All right.

71
00:03:10,995 --> 00:03:11,829
Mr. Tatsuki.

72
00:03:12,397 --> 00:03:13,464
Hello.

73
00:03:13,531 --> 00:03:15,133
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

74
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:16,534
Say hello.

75
00:03:17,969 --> 00:03:19,871
Hello, I'm Saku Sugitani.

76
00:03:19,937 --> 00:03:21,039
Hello.

77
00:03:22,173 --> 00:03:24,609
-Please sit.
-Thank you.

78
00:03:30,248 --> 00:03:32,750
He's currently a fifth grader
in elementary school,

79
00:03:32,817 --> 00:03:34,319
but starting around mid-April,

80
00:03:34,385 --> 00:03:36,587
he started taking days off of school.

81
00:03:36,654 --> 00:03:39,957
After the long holiday break,
he told me he doesn't want to go back.

82
00:03:41,192 --> 00:03:42,694
Did something happen at school?

83
00:03:44,796 --> 00:03:45,897
Not really.

84
00:03:47,065 --> 00:03:49,934
He doesn't seem to be having
any problems with his friends.

85
00:03:51,436 --> 00:03:53,104
You just don't want to go to school?

86
00:03:54,505 --> 00:03:55,707
It's a drag.

87
00:03:56,641 --> 00:03:57,775
A drag, huh.

88
00:03:58,343 --> 00:03:59,677
Yeah, school is such a drag.

89
00:04:00,345 --> 00:04:01,179
I totally get it.

90
00:04:02,447 --> 00:04:04,849
-Mr. Tatsuki.
-What?

91
00:04:04,916 --> 00:04:07,885
I happened to learn about Yukanai online.

92
00:04:07,952 --> 00:04:11,389
I thought that letting children
be independent and free

93
00:04:11,456 --> 00:04:13,891
might be the right approach
for my son right now.

94
00:04:13,958 --> 00:04:17,295
Yes, everyone here is certainly
doing what they want.

95
00:04:18,062 --> 00:04:20,465
When I asked him about it,
he said he wanted to come.

96
00:04:20,531 --> 00:04:21,599
I see.

97
00:04:23,534 --> 00:04:24,869
Do you play soccer?

98
00:04:28,406 --> 00:04:30,208
You like sports in general, right?

99
00:04:31,542 --> 00:04:32,377
Kind of…

100
00:04:33,544 --> 00:04:34,746
-Yeah.
-I see.

101
00:04:34,812 --> 00:04:36,647
He's pretty good with his studies too.

102
00:04:37,215 --> 00:04:40,518
Whoa, no way.
You're definitely popular, huh?

103
00:04:41,119 --> 00:04:42,754
-You are, huh?
-Mr. Tatsuki.

104
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,122
-What?
-Let's not say that.

105
00:04:44,188 --> 00:04:46,991
-Why? He's so impressive.
-But still…

106
00:04:47,058 --> 00:04:49,861
-There's no way he's not popular.
-That's not the issue.

107
00:04:49,927 --> 00:04:51,262
Your turn to serve.

108
00:04:52,063 --> 00:04:54,265
-Where did it go?
-Are you serious?

109
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:58,069
Let's play soccer.

110
00:04:58,136 --> 00:04:58,970
Yeah.

111
00:05:00,705 --> 00:05:03,274
We're going to play soccer now,
wanna join us?

112
00:05:03,341 --> 00:05:04,308
It'll be out in the yard.

113
00:05:08,813 --> 00:05:10,181
I'm okay right now.

114
00:05:10,248 --> 00:05:11,449
Okay.

115
00:05:11,516 --> 00:05:13,284
Come join us when you feel like it.

116
00:05:14,619 --> 00:05:15,453
Okay.

117
00:05:16,387 --> 00:05:17,622
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

118
00:05:17,688 --> 00:05:19,357
-Nice, nice.
-Yeah.

119
00:05:19,424 --> 00:05:20,758
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

120
00:05:27,565 --> 00:05:29,667
You can use anything here
however you like.

121
00:05:32,537 --> 00:05:34,505
Hey, let's play Bomb Busters.

122
00:05:37,442 --> 00:05:38,776
Okay.

123
00:05:38,843 --> 00:05:40,044
Let's play next time.

124
00:05:40,745 --> 00:05:41,746
Gaku, let's play this.

125
00:05:48,453 --> 00:05:50,154
What?

126
00:05:50,955 --> 00:05:52,990
What happened?

127
00:05:53,057 --> 00:05:54,258
-I'm sorry.
-What happened?

128
00:05:54,892 --> 00:05:55,760
I'm sorry.

129
00:05:55,827 --> 00:05:57,161
-Are you all right?
-Yeah.

130
00:05:57,762 --> 00:05:59,530
I'm sorry.

131
00:05:59,597 --> 00:06:00,431
Thank you.

132
00:06:00,932 --> 00:06:03,668
-Were you replacing the books?
-Yeah.

133
00:06:03,734 --> 00:06:05,136
Professor Mikumo

134
00:06:05,203 --> 00:06:07,371
brought us a bunch of old books
the other day.

135
00:06:11,676 --> 00:06:12,977
Do you like history?

136
00:06:14,378 --> 00:06:15,213
No…

137
00:06:16,347 --> 00:06:19,884
I don't know much about history.

138
00:06:20,751 --> 00:06:22,420
Are there any Sengoku warlords you like?

139
00:06:26,357 --> 00:06:29,227
-Nobunaga.
-Oh, I know a little about him.

140
00:06:30,628 --> 00:06:32,263
Who's this man?

141
00:06:32,330 --> 00:06:33,264
TALES OF THE STRONGEST SENGOKU WARLORDS

142
00:06:33,831 --> 00:06:34,799
Kuroda Kanbei.

143
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:38,169
Wow, you really know a lot!

144
00:06:44,475 --> 00:06:46,143
You can take that home.

145
00:06:47,078 --> 00:06:48,679
-Really?
-Yeah.

146
00:06:48,746 --> 00:06:50,481
I'm sure no one else will read it.

147
00:06:58,956 --> 00:07:00,224
I've got a good idea.

148
00:07:05,062 --> 00:07:07,265
-All right.
-What are you doing?

149
00:07:07,331 --> 00:07:09,066
I'm making a collage.

150
00:07:10,167 --> 00:07:11,669
-A collage?
-Yup.

151
00:07:12,436 --> 00:07:16,474
You just cut out images that you like

152
00:07:16,541 --> 00:07:18,242
and paste them together.

153
00:07:20,077 --> 00:07:23,080
By the way, those are collages
made by another student.

154
00:07:25,049 --> 00:07:26,317
Wow.

155
00:07:28,019 --> 00:07:28,853
Try it out.

156
00:07:37,094 --> 00:07:39,564
Which one should I choose?

157
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:40,498
SOCCER MANIA

158
00:07:50,408 --> 00:07:52,710
Hey, can you help me reach the top of

159
00:07:52,777 --> 00:07:54,845
-the bookshelf--
-Once you cut that out, paste it on here.

160
00:07:56,047 --> 00:07:56,881
-Um…
-How?

161
00:07:57,815 --> 00:07:59,917
-However you want to.
-Can you hear me?

162
00:07:59,984 --> 00:08:03,321
It's too high, and I can't reach it so…

163
00:08:03,387 --> 00:08:05,022
-Ms. Shizuku.
-I'll do this one.

164
00:08:05,089 --> 00:08:07,024
Can you bring more old magazines?

165
00:08:08,092 --> 00:08:09,827
Go get them yourself.

166
00:08:11,028 --> 00:08:11,862
What was that for?

167
00:08:14,298 --> 00:08:17,234
-Mr. Tatsuki.
-Just call me Tatsuki.

168
00:08:18,402 --> 00:08:21,405
-You have to be nicer to women.
-What?

169
00:08:22,173 --> 00:08:23,874
Oh, you mean about Ms. Shizuku?

170
00:08:23,941 --> 00:08:25,409
Yeah. She was mad.

171
00:08:25,476 --> 00:08:28,012
What? She was mad?

172
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:29,947
Really?

173
00:08:31,549 --> 00:08:32,817
You're so oblivious.

174
00:08:34,218 --> 00:08:35,519
I get that a lot.

175
00:08:36,854 --> 00:08:38,422
BATTLE OF KANEGASAKI

176
00:08:38,489 --> 00:08:39,490
All done.

177
00:08:41,492 --> 00:08:43,227
It turned out so powerful.

178
00:08:46,364 --> 00:08:48,866
What's happening in this scene?

179
00:08:51,068 --> 00:08:52,036
They're fighting.

180
00:08:54,372 --> 00:08:56,574
But they're getting pushed back
by the enemy.

181
00:08:56,641 --> 00:08:58,809
I see.

182
00:09:00,077 --> 00:09:00,911
Who's this?

183
00:09:02,179 --> 00:09:03,414
-Nobunaga.
-I thought so.

184
00:09:03,481 --> 00:09:04,849
He's so strong and amazing.

185
00:09:04,915 --> 00:09:05,950
Yeah, he's amazing.

186
00:09:13,024 --> 00:09:14,492
Hey, Tatsuki.

187
00:09:17,094 --> 00:09:19,497
Don't tell anyone
that I'm a history buff, okay?

188
00:09:20,731 --> 00:09:21,932
Okay.

189
00:09:36,447 --> 00:09:38,082
As for Thursday's Activity Day,

190
00:09:38,149 --> 00:09:39,950
we couldn't pick just one thing,

191
00:09:40,017 --> 00:09:41,519
so we'll be doing everything.

192
00:09:41,585 --> 00:09:42,953
It'll be like Sports Day.

193
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:45,423
Then let's play tug-of-war too.

194
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:48,859
I just got this rope. Look!

195
00:09:48,926 --> 00:09:50,728
No way!

196
00:09:50,795 --> 00:09:52,063
Where did you get that?

197
00:09:52,129 --> 00:09:53,664
Did you get it from a shrine?

198
00:09:53,731 --> 00:09:56,233
I guess it was being used
at the local festival,

199
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:57,334
but it's too old now.

200
00:09:57,902 --> 00:10:00,371
-Then let's do tug-of-war too.
-Okay.

201
00:10:01,138 --> 00:10:03,474
-Pull this, Soya.
-Okay.

202
00:10:03,541 --> 00:10:04,375
Come on.

203
00:10:04,809 --> 00:10:05,643
‎Wow.

204
00:10:08,579 --> 00:10:11,115
‎-Bye Professor.
‎-Bye

205
00:10:14,051 --> 00:10:15,286
Hey there.

206
00:10:15,352 --> 00:10:16,587
Hey.

207
00:10:16,654 --> 00:10:18,255
-A collage?
-Yes.

208
00:10:19,457 --> 00:10:21,525
A Sengoku warlord and soccer players.

209
00:10:21,592 --> 00:10:23,461
It's an interesting combination, isn't it?

210
00:10:24,595 --> 00:10:26,063
Who made this collage?

211
00:10:26,664 --> 00:10:28,632
He's a boy in fifth grade.

212
00:10:28,699 --> 00:10:31,402
He seems to be good at studies and sports,
and has friends too.

213
00:10:31,469 --> 00:10:33,437
But he refuses to go to school, right?

214
00:10:33,504 --> 00:10:34,805
-Yes.
-Why?

215
00:10:37,608 --> 00:10:39,410
-He said it's a drag.
-A drag?

216
00:10:40,678 --> 00:10:42,947
Does that mean he finds it tiring?

217
00:10:43,013 --> 00:10:45,950
No, how can I explain it…?

218
00:10:46,016 --> 00:10:48,152
Is it that he can't sum up
the energy to go?

219
00:10:49,887 --> 00:10:51,989
I think he considers it a hassle.

220
00:10:52,990 --> 00:10:55,793
-I see.
-What do you think about this?

221
00:11:00,431 --> 00:11:02,767
There's just one guy who's running away.

222
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:04,301
You're right.

223
00:11:04,368 --> 00:11:06,871
The boss has a really
intimidating presence, doesn't he?

224
00:11:07,972 --> 00:11:09,940
Does it represent someone?

225
00:11:10,641 --> 00:11:12,743
If it's not a friend,

226
00:11:13,410 --> 00:11:14,345
maybe

227
00:11:15,646 --> 00:11:17,181
a teacher, for example?

228
00:11:17,782 --> 00:11:19,049
That's a possibility.

229
00:11:19,116 --> 00:11:22,153
Kids sometimes stop going to school
when they don't get along with teachers.

230
00:11:22,219 --> 00:11:23,120
Yeah.

231
00:11:23,754 --> 00:11:26,090
Saku goes to Nishiogi Elementary School,

232
00:11:26,157 --> 00:11:28,793
so I'll try to find something out tomorrow

233
00:11:28,859 --> 00:11:31,028
when I go to submit
the academic progress report.

234
00:11:31,095 --> 00:11:32,463
You sure love schools, huh.

235
00:11:32,530 --> 00:11:34,632
It's not that I love it or anything.

236
00:11:34,698 --> 00:11:36,500
I hope you don't complicate things more.

237
00:11:36,567 --> 00:11:38,369
Then you want to just let things be?

238
00:11:40,504 --> 00:11:41,939
Tatsuki, you should go with her.

239
00:11:42,006 --> 00:11:44,708
-Oh, I can't tomorrow…
-You have plans?

240
00:11:45,876 --> 00:11:47,478
I have to catch
a different colored Pikachu.

241
00:11:48,045 --> 00:11:49,580
What?

242
00:11:49,647 --> 00:11:51,515
This is more important than that!

243
00:11:51,582 --> 00:11:52,950
I guess you can't cancel that.

244
00:11:54,185 --> 00:11:55,452
Are you serious?

245
00:11:56,353 --> 00:11:58,122
NISHIOGI ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

246
00:11:58,689 --> 00:12:01,225
I can't think of the reason why either.

247
00:12:01,292 --> 00:12:05,462
Sugitani is a very popular
and outgoing student in our class.

248
00:12:05,529 --> 00:12:08,065
He started missing school
around mid-April, right?

249
00:12:09,099 --> 00:12:10,701
At first it was just Mondays.

250
00:12:10,768 --> 00:12:14,104
Then Mondays and Wednesdays.
It gradually kept increasing.

251
00:12:14,672 --> 00:12:15,940
I see.

252
00:12:16,006 --> 00:12:16,907
Oh, sorry,

253
00:12:16,974 --> 00:12:19,143
-I have to practice for Sports Day.
-Sorry.

254
00:12:19,210 --> 00:12:21,178
-Thank you.
-No problem.

255
00:12:24,415 --> 00:12:25,449
CLASS SCHEDULE

256
00:12:25,516 --> 00:12:28,385
Mondays and Wednesdays.

257
00:12:28,452 --> 00:12:29,353
MONDAY - PE

258
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:30,821
WEDNESDAY

259
00:12:30,888 --> 00:12:32,356
PE

260
00:12:34,859 --> 00:12:37,962
All right, stop. One, two.

261
00:12:38,028 --> 00:12:39,897
Hey, you stepped out of line.

262
00:12:40,464 --> 00:12:41,532
Let's do it one more time.

263
00:12:42,399 --> 00:12:44,001
Step in place.

264
00:12:44,068 --> 00:12:45,703
It looks like Sports Day is in two weeks.

265
00:12:46,804 --> 00:12:49,607
I wonder if there's any point
in practicing marching.

266
00:12:50,407 --> 00:12:52,543
It's satisfying to watch
when they're in sync, isn't it?

267
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:54,645
-One, two.
-You think so?

268
00:12:55,846 --> 00:13:00,184
I wonder if Saku
didn't like the Sports Day practice.

269
00:13:00,251 --> 00:13:02,219
-But he's good at all sports, right?
-Yes.

270
00:13:02,953 --> 00:13:05,656
In that case, Sports Day is actually

271
00:13:05,723 --> 00:13:07,658
a great opportunity for him to shine.

272
00:13:07,725 --> 00:13:09,560
But he started skipping school on days

273
00:13:09,627 --> 00:13:11,095
when they had PE,

274
00:13:11,161 --> 00:13:13,097
and when the Sports Day practices began.

275
00:13:14,765 --> 00:13:16,867
Step in place.

276
00:13:16,934 --> 00:13:18,102
Doesn't that teacher

277
00:13:18,168 --> 00:13:21,238
-kind of remind you of Nobunaga?
-One, two.

278
00:13:21,305 --> 00:13:23,407
One, two! Hey, you're doing it
the wrong way!

279
00:13:23,474 --> 00:13:26,477
One, two.
Keep looking at everyone around you!

280
00:13:26,543 --> 00:13:28,812
-Oh yes…
-One, two!

281
00:13:31,782 --> 00:13:34,818
Excuse me. Sorry to bother you
when you're so busy.

282
00:13:34,885 --> 00:13:37,821
I'm Aomine from
the alternative school, Yukanai.

283
00:13:39,256 --> 00:13:41,292
-I'm Tatsuki.
-How can I help you?

284
00:13:42,092 --> 00:13:45,496
I'd like to ask you a few questions
about Saku Sugitani.

285
00:13:47,197 --> 00:13:50,000
I'm very worried about Sugitani too.

286
00:13:50,567 --> 00:13:52,670
How is he doing at your school?

287
00:13:52,736 --> 00:13:55,506
Oh, he's doing well.

288
00:13:55,572 --> 00:13:57,508
I'm so glad.

289
00:13:57,574 --> 00:13:59,743
He was always so cheerful.

290
00:14:03,347 --> 00:14:05,149
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

291
00:14:05,215 --> 00:14:06,050
Good day.

292
00:14:08,619 --> 00:14:11,188
<i>He ended up being a nice guy, huh?</i>

293
00:14:11,755 --> 00:14:13,891
You shouldn't have judged
a book by its cover.

294
00:14:13,958 --> 00:14:16,593
Hey, you thought he was scary too,
didn't you?

295
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:17,962
No, I did not.

296
00:14:18,028 --> 00:14:18,963
So unfair.

297
00:14:21,598 --> 00:14:25,069
I was absolutely convinced that
the Sports Day practice was the issue.

298
00:14:25,135 --> 00:14:26,570
I think you've got it right.

299
00:14:26,637 --> 00:14:28,138
You think so too?

300
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:30,774
I got this.

301
00:14:30,841 --> 00:14:32,810
-The program for Sports Day?
-Yup.

302
00:14:32,876 --> 00:14:34,011
SPORTS DAY

303
00:14:34,078 --> 00:14:36,547
Which one was Saku planning
to participate in?

304
00:14:36,613 --> 00:14:40,851
He was chosen for the fifth-grade events,
and also as a runner for the relay team.

305
00:14:40,918 --> 00:14:41,952
I see.

306
00:14:42,019 --> 00:14:43,654
SPORTS DAY

307
00:14:48,025 --> 00:14:49,193
All right!

308
00:14:49,259 --> 00:14:51,395
-Damn it.
-He's so good.

309
00:14:51,462 --> 00:14:52,663
Saku, you're so good.

310
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:53,831
What's the trick?

311
00:14:54,898 --> 00:14:57,968
Don't just move your arm,
but put your weight into it like this.

312
00:14:58,035 --> 00:15:01,071
-You're good at everything, Saku.
-Kind of.

313
00:15:01,705 --> 00:15:04,074
All right everyone.
Let's start cleaning up.

314
00:15:05,342 --> 00:15:06,944
-Okay.
-All right!

315
00:15:07,011 --> 00:15:09,246
-Good job.
-I did it.

316
00:15:09,313 --> 00:15:10,681
-I did it.
-You're a genius.

317
00:15:10,748 --> 00:15:11,915
I did it.

318
00:15:11,982 --> 00:15:13,017
Let's clean up.

319
00:15:13,083 --> 00:15:14,485
-No, one more time.
-Clean it up.

320
00:15:14,551 --> 00:15:15,986
Let's play this other game.

321
00:15:16,053 --> 00:15:17,521
-What?
-Let's play this game.

322
00:15:17,588 --> 00:15:19,189
I want to play Jenga.

323
00:15:19,256 --> 00:15:20,691
What about Dominion?

324
00:15:20,758 --> 00:15:22,326
Let's all clean up.

325
00:15:22,393 --> 00:15:24,595
Everyone please take
the Activity Day flyer

326
00:15:24,661 --> 00:15:26,397
when you leave.

327
00:15:26,463 --> 00:15:29,366
-Okay.
-Is Tatsuki going too?

328
00:15:29,433 --> 00:15:31,568
Yeah. You'll be going too, right?

329
00:15:32,136 --> 00:15:33,904
Yeah, I'm looking forward to it.

330
00:15:33,971 --> 00:15:35,506
Take this home with you.

331
00:15:35,572 --> 00:15:36,974
Thank you.

332
00:15:37,041 --> 00:15:40,511
-Oh, wow, how exciting.
-Take this home with you.

333
00:15:40,577 --> 00:15:41,845
-Thanks.
-Take care.

334
00:15:41,912 --> 00:15:43,747
-Bye.
-Bye.

335
00:15:47,785 --> 00:15:50,487
-Go Red!
-Game start!

336
00:15:51,889 --> 00:15:53,357
‎-Gaku!
‎-Tatsuki!

337
00:15:53,424 --> 00:15:54,892
Nice pass!

338
00:16:02,699 --> 00:16:04,902
Go, go!

339
00:16:07,337 --> 00:16:08,639
Start.

340
00:16:10,741 --> 00:16:12,176
‎We can do it.

341
00:16:16,146 --> 00:16:17,781
Make sure you score.

342
00:16:17,848 --> 00:16:20,317
-You can do it, Tatsuki.
-Go.

343
00:16:20,384 --> 00:16:21,285
Go!

344
00:16:35,065 --> 00:16:37,267
Don't get too depressed about it.

345
00:16:55,119 --> 00:16:56,120
Saku.

346
00:16:57,788 --> 00:16:58,789
You're not going to dance?

347
00:17:01,758 --> 00:17:05,395
<i>If they try to go into defense here,</i>
<i>then that will cause…</i>

348
00:17:05,462 --> 00:17:06,597
-Tatsuki.
-Yeah?

349
00:17:07,798 --> 00:17:09,433
Was it okay for you to leave?

350
00:17:10,567 --> 00:17:11,735
The truth is,

351
00:17:12,236 --> 00:17:14,304
I'm not very good at ball games.

352
00:17:15,539 --> 00:17:16,807
My penalty kick was terrible, huh?

353
00:17:17,474 --> 00:17:18,709
Yeah.

354
00:17:18,775 --> 00:17:20,110
I lost motivation after that.

355
00:17:20,711 --> 00:17:22,446
If I did something that embarrassing

356
00:17:22,513 --> 00:17:23,914
-I wouldn't be able to live.
-Hey.

357
00:17:25,983 --> 00:17:29,353
I'm not like you who can do everything.

358
00:17:35,125 --> 00:17:37,928
I can't dance.

359
00:17:41,465 --> 00:17:42,533
I see.

360
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:45,235
I can't do the dance

361
00:17:46,770 --> 00:17:47,938
for Sports Day.

362
00:17:48,438 --> 00:17:52,176
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

363
00:17:52,242 --> 00:17:54,945
One, two, three, four, five, six…

364
00:17:55,012 --> 00:17:56,747
<i>I can never remember the steps.</i>

365
00:17:58,248 --> 00:17:59,349
<i>Once I fall out of sync,</i>

366
00:17:59,983 --> 00:18:01,652
<i>I can't keep up anymore.</i>

367
00:18:04,087 --> 00:18:06,056
I just keep feeling
more and more pathetic.

368
00:18:10,727 --> 00:18:11,929
I see.

369
00:18:13,697 --> 00:18:15,165
That's tough.

370
00:18:27,044 --> 00:18:28,812
Just ask to be removed from the dance.

371
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:30,414
What?

372
00:18:31,114 --> 00:18:32,583
No need to force yourself to do it.

373
00:18:36,053 --> 00:18:37,554
Everyone has to participate in the dance.

374
00:18:38,121 --> 00:18:40,591
But you still want to compete
in the other events, right?

375
00:18:41,158 --> 00:18:43,594
Isn't it frustrating to have to sit
everything out just for that?

376
00:18:51,201 --> 00:18:52,436
If you want to run away,

377
00:18:53,337 --> 00:18:54,471
it's okay to do so.

378
00:18:55,939 --> 00:18:58,308
I just ran away too.

379
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:04,114
But…

380
00:19:06,049 --> 00:19:08,552
I can't admit to everyone now
that I'm bad at dancing.

381
00:19:10,921 --> 00:19:13,056
Because you're known for
being good at everything?

382
00:19:16,426 --> 00:19:17,327
Yeah.

383
00:19:25,736 --> 00:19:26,670
What do you want to do?

384
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:32,509
You can choose to do
whatever you want, Saku.

385
00:19:48,959 --> 00:19:49,960
I don't want…

386
00:19:56,166 --> 00:19:57,401
to do the dance.

387
00:20:10,514 --> 00:20:11,682
I went to his school.

388
00:20:11,748 --> 00:20:14,351
They said Saku doesn't have
to participate in the dance.

389
00:20:18,889 --> 00:20:22,292
Um… I actually went out of my way
to visit his school

390
00:20:22,359 --> 00:20:24,227
after Activity Day ended.

391
00:20:25,395 --> 00:20:26,463
Thanks.

392
00:20:27,864 --> 00:20:30,033
I'm glad you can benefit
from my love for school.

393
00:20:34,971 --> 00:20:36,039
What?

394
00:20:37,874 --> 00:20:40,911
I'm sure schools love you too,
Ms. Shizuku.

395
00:20:42,212 --> 00:20:43,313
Forget it.

396
00:20:45,916 --> 00:20:48,418
Thank you. I'll relay the news to Saku.

397
00:20:49,686 --> 00:20:51,888
Thank you. Bye.

398
00:21:11,842 --> 00:21:13,076
Good morning.

399
00:21:13,143 --> 00:21:14,745
Hey, Saku.

400
00:21:14,811 --> 00:21:16,880
Saku is here. Let's play Ruler Wars.

401
00:21:18,648 --> 00:21:20,417
-Yeah, let's.
-Are you better now?

402
00:21:21,351 --> 00:21:23,754
Yup. I made a complete recovery!

403
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:27,324
Right, left, hop, hop, hop.

404
00:21:27,391 --> 00:21:30,861
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

405
00:21:30,927 --> 00:21:33,029
Hey, did you make your mask?

406
00:21:33,597 --> 00:21:36,366
-A mask?
-All right, let's take a break.

407
00:21:36,433 --> 00:21:38,268
-No…
-Make sure to stay hydrated.

408
00:21:38,335 --> 00:21:41,271
I'm going to the restroom.

409
00:21:41,338 --> 00:21:44,374
Hey Saku. Why are you just watching?

410
00:21:46,810 --> 00:21:47,644
Just because…

411
00:21:49,212 --> 00:21:50,247
I'm going to the restroom.

412
00:21:54,217 --> 00:21:57,988
Left, right, left, hop…

413
00:22:13,770 --> 00:22:15,705
YUKANAI
NOW ACCEPTING NEW STUDENTS!

414
00:22:15,772 --> 00:22:19,509
Yes, Saku is here, so please don't worry.

415
00:22:20,076 --> 00:22:23,113
Yes. Goodbye.

416
00:22:23,914 --> 00:22:25,449
-Was that his school?
-Yeah,

417
00:22:25,515 --> 00:22:27,584
it seems like he suddenly left
during PE.

418
00:22:30,220 --> 00:22:31,588
I see.

419
00:22:41,965 --> 00:22:44,100
You left school without telling anyone?

420
00:22:47,304 --> 00:22:48,271
It's boring to just watch.

421
00:22:48,905 --> 00:22:50,574
Yeah, it's boring, huh?

422
00:22:51,675 --> 00:22:53,777
But if you leave without a word,
everyone will worry.

423
00:22:54,611 --> 00:22:55,745
I'm sorry.

424
00:22:56,613 --> 00:22:58,215
Want to make another collage?

425
00:23:01,751 --> 00:23:03,520
-I have to return the books I borrowed.
-What?

426
00:23:04,254 --> 00:23:06,289
Oh, you can have those old books.

427
00:23:06,356 --> 00:23:07,557
But I read them all.

428
00:23:13,129 --> 00:23:15,632
LET'S MAKE A MASK FOR THE DANCE!

429
00:23:17,634 --> 00:23:19,569
Apparently, it's a mask for the dance.

430
00:23:22,572 --> 00:23:23,406
I don't need that.

431
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:31,147
Want to make it?

432
00:23:32,115 --> 00:23:32,949
What?

433
00:23:35,819 --> 00:23:38,755
-He sat out on practice, but left mid-way?
-Yes.

434
00:23:39,256 --> 00:23:41,925
But we're not really sure why.

435
00:23:41,992 --> 00:23:45,061
Maybe he started hating himself
for running away.

436
00:23:46,363 --> 00:23:48,298
That's a possibility too.

437
00:23:48,865 --> 00:23:52,702
He tends to be a perfectionist.

438
00:23:54,004 --> 00:23:56,273
Since I used to work
as a middle school teacher,

439
00:23:56,339 --> 00:23:58,575
I tend to think that
you have to challenge all things,

440
00:23:58,642 --> 00:24:01,511
even if it's something you're not
particularly good at.

441
00:24:01,578 --> 00:24:02,546
Yes.

442
00:24:03,213 --> 00:24:07,217
I think overcoming difficulties
is also a part of education.

443
00:24:08,752 --> 00:24:12,722
But if it's going to break their spirit,
then it's better

444
00:24:12,789 --> 00:24:14,591
not to push them too hard.

445
00:24:17,394 --> 00:24:19,462
It's tough, isn't it?

446
00:24:22,732 --> 00:24:25,368
-Done.
-Let me see.

447
00:24:25,969 --> 00:24:27,737
Ta-da. Guess who this is.

448
00:24:27,804 --> 00:24:28,939
A hint. He's a soccer player.

449
00:24:29,005 --> 00:24:30,340
I wonder who it is.

450
00:24:32,309 --> 00:24:33,310
Ramos.

451
00:24:33,376 --> 00:24:35,312
-Who is that?
-You don't know Ramos?

452
00:24:35,879 --> 00:24:38,348
Seriously? Okay then…

453
00:24:40,850 --> 00:24:42,152
Is it Messi?

454
00:24:42,218 --> 00:24:43,820
-Bingo.
-Yes.

455
00:24:43,887 --> 00:24:44,754
Let's see yours.

456
00:24:46,923 --> 00:24:48,091
Ta-da.

457
00:24:49,526 --> 00:24:50,994
It looks just like you.

458
00:24:51,061 --> 00:24:52,228
Right?

459
00:24:53,063 --> 00:24:55,131
Let's draw on the other side too.

460
00:24:55,799 --> 00:24:57,000
-The other side?
-Yeah.

461
00:24:57,067 --> 00:24:59,169
For the other side…

462
00:25:00,103 --> 00:25:03,540
Let's draw a secret side of us,
one we usually never show anyone.

463
00:25:12,949 --> 00:25:14,117
Are you crying?

464
00:25:15,986 --> 00:25:18,788
You usually don't want anyone
to see you crying, right?

465
00:25:23,159 --> 00:25:26,229
Is that a Sengoku warlord?

466
00:25:27,030 --> 00:25:28,365
Nobunaga?

467
00:25:28,431 --> 00:25:29,532
Bingo.

468
00:25:29,599 --> 00:25:30,900
Why did you choose Nobunaga?

469
00:25:34,137 --> 00:25:35,205
I wonder why.

470
00:25:39,075 --> 00:25:41,044
Oh, because it's a secret
that you're a history buff?

471
00:25:42,312 --> 00:25:44,814
Maybe that's it.
After all, it doesn't fit my image.

472
00:25:47,217 --> 00:25:48,785
Both the front and back turned out great.

473
00:25:52,155 --> 00:25:54,724
Saku, let's head home.

474
00:25:58,395 --> 00:26:00,163
It's okay. I'll clean up. You can go.

475
00:26:00,964 --> 00:26:01,865
-Thanks.
-Sure.

476
00:26:13,309 --> 00:26:14,778
-Tatsuki.
-Yeah?

477
00:26:18,314 --> 00:26:19,282
I'm going

478
00:26:20,550 --> 00:26:21,718
to try the dance after all.

479
00:26:22,686 --> 00:26:23,520
What?

480
00:26:23,586 --> 00:26:25,388
I'll practice on my own

481
00:26:26,756 --> 00:26:28,091
and learn the dance by Sports Day.

482
00:26:32,262 --> 00:26:33,096
Okay.

483
00:26:45,508 --> 00:26:46,943
-A mask?
-Yeah.

484
00:26:47,010 --> 00:26:50,113
He made the mask
that's going to be used for the dance,

485
00:26:50,180 --> 00:26:52,682
but it seems
that really got him motivated.

486
00:26:52,749 --> 00:26:54,184
What kind of a mask was it?

487
00:26:54,951 --> 00:26:57,353
Messi is on the front,
and Nobunaga is on the back.

488
00:26:58,321 --> 00:26:59,956
Apparently, Saku admires both of them.

489
00:27:00,023 --> 00:27:01,524
I see.

490
00:27:02,225 --> 00:27:03,993
This is Mr. Tatsuki's mask.

491
00:27:04,828 --> 00:27:06,029
Don't bring that out…

492
00:27:07,831 --> 00:27:09,566
Oh? Why is he crying?

493
00:27:09,632 --> 00:27:10,900
Well,

494
00:27:11,701 --> 00:27:13,703
it's a face I don't want to show others.

495
00:27:13,770 --> 00:27:15,705
I see.

496
00:27:16,606 --> 00:27:18,274
When doing art therapy,

497
00:27:18,341 --> 00:27:20,176
people create pieces
that distinguish between

498
00:27:20,810 --> 00:27:24,614
their outward self and the self
they wish to keep hidden deep inside.

499
00:27:27,283 --> 00:27:28,118
Huh?

500
00:27:28,752 --> 00:27:30,587
Mr. Tatsuki,

501
00:27:30,653 --> 00:27:32,889
-what are you keeping hidden inside?
-Stop that.

502
00:27:32,956 --> 00:27:36,359
By the way,
can you stop calling me "Mr." please?

503
00:27:37,093 --> 00:27:38,161
It seems like

504
00:27:38,228 --> 00:27:40,663
art therapy really does work, doesn't it?

505
00:27:40,730 --> 00:27:42,732
Saku seems to have been motivated.

506
00:27:43,433 --> 00:27:44,434
What do you think?

507
00:27:46,069 --> 00:27:50,206
But perhaps
even he himself doesn't realize

508
00:27:50,273 --> 00:27:52,809
the true feelings he has
deep within his heart.

509
00:27:53,443 --> 00:27:54,778
I see.

510
00:27:55,345 --> 00:27:58,515
If I recall correctly, he used Nobunaga
in that collage the other day too.

511
00:27:58,581 --> 00:28:02,819
I was under the impression
that he was a frightening figure to Saku,

512
00:28:02,886 --> 00:28:04,220
but he actually seems to like him.

513
00:28:04,954 --> 00:28:08,224
In that case, you ought to delve deeper

514
00:28:08,291 --> 00:28:10,693
into the thing that he likes.

515
00:28:12,028 --> 00:28:13,963
You just might discover something new.

516
00:28:15,331 --> 00:28:16,332
Okay.

517
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:21,104
<i>Right, left, hop, hop, hop.</i>

518
00:28:32,549 --> 00:28:35,919
<i>Ready? Let's start.</i>

519
00:28:36,619 --> 00:28:39,956
<i>Five, six, seven, eight.</i>
<i>One, two, three, four…</i>

520
00:29:39,082 --> 00:29:42,952
Three, four, five, six…

521
00:29:46,890 --> 00:29:48,524
Let's do it again.

522
00:29:52,095 --> 00:29:53,296
YUKANAI

523
00:29:58,701 --> 00:29:59,802
Good morning, Saku.

524
00:30:03,873 --> 00:30:04,707
Where's Tatsuki?

525
00:30:05,508 --> 00:30:06,643
-I'll go call him.
-No…

526
00:30:09,312 --> 00:30:10,146
It's okay.

527
00:30:21,024 --> 00:30:21,958
What're you doing?

528
00:30:25,295 --> 00:30:27,363
I'm not very good with history,

529
00:30:27,430 --> 00:30:30,667
so I tried to study by putting myself
in Nobunaga’s shoes. I splurged on this.

530
00:30:32,001 --> 00:30:32,835
You bought it?

531
00:30:36,706 --> 00:30:39,142
By the way, Lord, what is the matter?

532
00:30:50,653 --> 00:30:51,487
We have

533
00:30:52,889 --> 00:30:55,825
a full dance rehearsal
this afternoon, but…

534
00:30:55,892 --> 00:30:57,894
Sports Day is coming up, huh?

535
00:31:00,396 --> 00:31:01,631
I'm scared.

536
00:31:02,398 --> 00:31:03,700
You practiced, right?

537
00:31:04,667 --> 00:31:05,501
But

538
00:31:06,102 --> 00:31:07,403
I've only practiced on my own.

539
00:31:07,470 --> 00:31:10,406
It might be hard
to dance along with everyone, huh?

540
00:31:12,141 --> 00:31:13,209
That's what scares me.

541
00:31:14,744 --> 00:31:15,979
Do you want to sit out?

542
00:31:17,814 --> 00:31:19,415
You can run away if you want.

543
00:31:19,482 --> 00:31:22,385
But that just doesn't fit my image.

544
00:31:23,386 --> 00:31:24,554
I’m supposed to be strong

545
00:31:25,221 --> 00:31:26,756
and able to do anything.

546
00:31:28,191 --> 00:31:29,125
Why?

547
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:32,095
Why?

548
00:31:35,164 --> 00:31:36,065
If I can't do it,

549
00:31:37,500 --> 00:31:39,035
everyone will be disappointed in me.

550
00:31:40,737 --> 00:31:42,071
I'll look lame too.

551
00:31:44,807 --> 00:31:46,542
That's just not who I am.

552
00:31:47,677 --> 00:31:48,578
That's why

553
00:31:49,479 --> 00:31:52,281
you have to be strong like Nobunaga?

554
00:31:54,650 --> 00:31:55,518
Yeah.

555
00:32:00,156 --> 00:32:01,691
But apparently,

556
00:32:02,358 --> 00:32:04,394
Nobunaga actually ran away
from a battle once.

557
00:32:09,032 --> 00:32:12,135
This image of Nobunaga
that you pasted on here,

558
00:32:12,201 --> 00:32:15,104
was taken from an illustration
of the Battle of Kanegasaki, huh?

559
00:32:15,171 --> 00:32:16,072
BATTLE OF KANEGASAKI

560
00:32:16,139 --> 00:32:18,074
I figured that out yesterday
after studying.

561
00:32:19,108 --> 00:32:20,610
I didn't even notice that.

562
00:32:21,377 --> 00:32:23,513
The Battle of Kanegasaki is referred to as

563
00:32:23,579 --> 00:32:25,782
the "battle of the forced retreat",
isn't it?

564
00:32:30,286 --> 00:32:31,821
In 1570,

565
00:32:31,888 --> 00:32:34,857
Nobunaga laid siege to Kanegasaki Castle,

566
00:32:34,924 --> 00:32:36,592
but after being betrayed by Azai Nagamasa,

567
00:32:37,160 --> 00:32:38,761
he had to flee in order to survive.

568
00:32:40,163 --> 00:32:41,798
What do you think

569
00:32:42,365 --> 00:32:44,367
of Nobunaga for retreating? Was he lame?

570
00:32:47,103 --> 00:32:48,071
If it was me

571
00:32:48,838 --> 00:32:49,939
I'd be a bit embarrassed.

572
00:32:51,574 --> 00:32:52,809
I see.

573
00:32:52,875 --> 00:32:53,709
But

574
00:32:55,211 --> 00:32:56,312
I don't think

575
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:58,314
he's lame.

576
00:33:02,118 --> 00:33:04,087
It's kind of cool

577
00:33:04,153 --> 00:33:05,988
how he bares all his weaknesses, huh?

578
00:33:23,339 --> 00:33:24,640
Saku, you can become

579
00:33:25,608 --> 00:33:26,676
Nobunaga too.

580
00:34:59,368 --> 00:35:01,437
Saku, let's play soccer.

581
00:35:01,504 --> 00:35:02,905
-Let's go.
-Let's play.

582
00:35:02,972 --> 00:35:03,806
Wait.

583
00:35:05,841 --> 00:35:06,776
Sorry.

584
00:35:09,212 --> 00:35:11,447
Can you help me practice the dance?

585
00:35:13,783 --> 00:35:16,552
I couldn't get all the moves
by watching the video.

586
00:35:19,255 --> 00:35:20,323
Sure.

587
00:35:20,389 --> 00:35:21,257
He took days off.

588
00:35:21,824 --> 00:35:22,925
Yeah, so we'll help you.

589
00:35:23,926 --> 00:35:24,794
Thanks.

590
00:35:25,328 --> 00:35:27,663
Right, left,

591
00:35:27,730 --> 00:35:29,465
down, and tap.

592
00:35:29,532 --> 00:35:31,934
Get up.

593
00:35:32,001 --> 00:35:34,804
Touch and turn. Right…

594
00:35:34,870 --> 00:35:36,672
-Sorry, one more time.
-Sure.

595
00:35:37,273 --> 00:35:38,641
Let's review the previous moves too.

596
00:35:41,911 --> 00:35:42,945
What's the matter?

597
00:35:44,180 --> 00:35:45,014
Hey,

598
00:35:46,215 --> 00:35:48,284
what do you think of me
being a bad dancer?

599
00:35:49,085 --> 00:35:50,052
Why this all of a sudden?

600
00:35:50,886 --> 00:35:52,255
I have no sense of rhythm,

601
00:35:53,289 --> 00:35:54,657
and I'm stiff…

602
00:35:56,659 --> 00:35:57,627
Isn't that lame?

603
00:35:58,761 --> 00:35:59,795
Not really.

604
00:36:01,297 --> 00:36:03,332
But I'm known as someone
who can do anything.

605
00:36:03,933 --> 00:36:04,767
Huh?

606
00:36:05,735 --> 00:36:07,870
-Is that right?
-What?

607
00:36:07,937 --> 00:36:10,539
We don't think you're perfect or anything.

608
00:36:10,606 --> 00:36:11,807
Yeah.

609
00:36:11,874 --> 00:36:13,309
-What?
-Yeah,

610
00:36:13,376 --> 00:36:15,745
because you can be pretty kooky.

611
00:36:15,811 --> 00:36:16,979
Yeah, totally.

612
00:36:18,147 --> 00:36:19,949
No way. Kooky? Me?

613
00:36:20,016 --> 00:36:21,684
For example,

614
00:36:21,751 --> 00:36:25,321
when it was music class,
you went to the home economics room.

615
00:36:25,388 --> 00:36:29,292
First of all, the fact
that you think you're perfect…

616
00:36:29,358 --> 00:36:30,192
Means you're kooky.

617
00:36:31,560 --> 00:36:32,461
Seriously?

618
00:36:33,763 --> 00:36:35,865
That's how I was coming across
to everyone?

619
00:36:35,931 --> 00:36:39,101
But you guys haven't figured out
that I'm a history buff, right?

620
00:36:43,539 --> 00:36:45,975
-Who cares if everyone knows?
-Yeah.

621
00:36:46,042 --> 00:36:47,076
By the way,

622
00:36:47,143 --> 00:36:49,412
let's practice, or you'll really be lame.

623
00:36:50,546 --> 00:36:52,815
Sorry, can we start from the top again?

624
00:36:52,882 --> 00:36:53,716
Okay.

625
00:36:53,783 --> 00:36:55,618
-Ready?
-Yeah.

626
00:36:55,685 --> 00:36:57,320
Let's start.

627
00:36:57,386 --> 00:37:00,790
One, two, three, four…

628
00:37:00,856 --> 00:37:03,492
Walk in place. Begin.

629
00:37:03,559 --> 00:37:04,927
One, two.

630
00:37:04,994 --> 00:37:08,030
Next up is a dance performance
by the fifth graders.

631
00:37:08,097 --> 00:37:10,299
It's called, "Dancing

632
00:37:10,366 --> 00:37:11,367
As My Character."

633
00:37:12,401 --> 00:37:13,536
-Where is he?
-I see him.

634
00:37:13,602 --> 00:37:15,304
Where? Point to him.

635
00:37:16,038 --> 00:37:17,406
-Oh, there he is.
-That's him.

636
00:37:17,473 --> 00:37:18,607
Good luck.

637
00:37:18,674 --> 00:37:19,508
Oh.

638
00:37:19,575 --> 00:37:20,509
Hello.

639
00:37:21,410 --> 00:37:24,447
-Hello.
-Saku is over there.

640
00:37:24,513 --> 00:37:26,816
-Oh, I see him. Thank you.
-He's Messi.

641
00:37:26,882 --> 00:37:28,050
One, two.

642
00:39:54,830 --> 00:39:56,599
Saku!

643
00:39:59,168 --> 00:40:00,503
You can do it!

644
00:40:05,241 --> 00:40:06,108
Tatsuki.

645
00:40:33,903 --> 00:40:35,304
‎All right.

646
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:39,001
Good job!

647
00:42:40,629 --> 00:42:41,563
Tatsuki.

648
00:42:44,400 --> 00:42:45,367
You came.

649
00:42:46,335 --> 00:42:47,302
Good job.

650
00:42:48,037 --> 00:42:49,338
I messed up.

651
00:42:50,839 --> 00:42:52,274
But it was very you, Saku.

652
00:42:52,841 --> 00:42:54,076
What's that supposed to mean?

653
00:42:55,110 --> 00:42:56,445
You were cool,

654
00:42:57,479 --> 00:42:58,480
but also endearing.

655
00:42:59,648 --> 00:43:00,549
That's not my image.

656
00:43:01,617 --> 00:43:03,419
But I'll go with a new image from now on.

657
00:43:05,054 --> 00:43:08,424
But don't get tied down by your image.
It's fine for you to be yourself.

658
00:43:14,730 --> 00:43:16,465
But you're maintaining your image too.

659
00:43:16,532 --> 00:43:17,666
What?

660
00:43:17,733 --> 00:43:19,568
On the surface, you're always smiling

661
00:43:20,335 --> 00:43:22,271
but inside, there's darkness, right?

662
00:43:25,774 --> 00:43:27,409
I don't have a hidden side.

663
00:43:27,476 --> 00:43:29,044
There's definitely darkness to you.

664
00:43:29,111 --> 00:43:30,579
-You think so?
-Yeah.

665
00:43:31,346 --> 00:43:33,882
No need to force a smile
when you're feeling down.

666
00:43:33,949 --> 00:43:35,350
What the hell?

667
00:43:35,417 --> 00:43:36,585
Can I go visit you again?

668
00:43:37,152 --> 00:43:38,420
Of course.

669
00:43:38,487 --> 00:43:39,321
Bye.

670
00:43:40,255 --> 00:43:41,156
Bye.

671
00:43:42,024 --> 00:43:44,593
-See you.
-Bye.

672
00:44:17,226 --> 00:44:20,395
<i>Sora, staying holed up like that</i>
<i>isn't going to solve anything, is it?</i>

673
00:44:21,096 --> 00:44:21,930
Are you listening?

674
00:44:23,465 --> 00:44:24,933
-Sora.
-That's enough.

675
00:44:25,000 --> 00:44:27,703
-Go to work.
-Sora, open the door.

676
00:44:29,905 --> 00:44:31,740
-Come out here.
-No.

677
00:44:31,807 --> 00:44:34,476
Stop it. That's enough. Just stop it.

678
00:44:36,011 --> 00:44:36,845
Sora!

679
00:45:03,071 --> 00:45:04,573
PREVIEW OF THE NEXT EPISODE

680
00:45:04,640 --> 00:45:05,641
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

681
00:45:05,707 --> 00:45:07,009
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita

